BEGIN_DESC
ORO LIGHTS TEST - an automatic twelve-case tour of the local-light and shadow work.

Load it and watch: the script spawns lamp posts and extra vessels around the DeltaGlider,
runs each case for about half a minute with the camera orbiting, and says on screen what
you should be seeing, which Launchpad row the case needs, and what the client's own debug
line should read. Everything it spawns is deleted at the end; your DeltaGlider is untouched.

  T        skip to the next case
  R        go back one case
  Ctrl+P   pause (the sequence pauses with the sim)

The cases: one spot; the DG's own landing light; two spots; four and six in a fan; a cluster
sharing one map; more lights than maps; a stadium flood; a point light in a ring of casters;
spots ranking before points; sixteen lights at once; and the same scene by day.

FOR A FULL PASS set, in the Launchpad's Video tab, Advanced setup: Local lights 16x Full,
Spot light shadows 6 spot maps, Point light shadows Cube, Terrain and world shadows
Cascaded (ORO). The title card reads your settings back and warns about any row a case
needs and does not have - so it is worth running whatever your settings are.

IF YOU ARE REPORTING SOMETHING, say which case number it was, send an UNPAUSED screenshot
or the video, and set ShadowDebug = 1 in D3D9Client.cfg first: the client then logs a line
a second and the rig puts it straight into the caption.

Needs the LuaInline module ticked in the Launchpad's Modules tab.
END_DESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
